On Wed, 22 Sep 2004, Boudewijn Waijers wrote:
> Philipp Lucas wrote:
> > Creatures heal 1 hp per 20 moves, and they can recover from being
> > blind, confused or stunned.
> But as I understand from other replies, this does not work with
> creatures you left behind on a level while you're healing yourself on
> another level, which was what we were talking about.

Yes it does work, this is what mon_catchup_elapsed_time in dog.c does:
When the character reenters a level, it computes, among other things, how
much the monsters have healed up in the meantime. (See the last lines of
the quoted function:

        /* recover lost hit points */
        if (!regenerates(mtmp->data)) imv /= 20;
        if (mtmp->mhp + imv >= mtmp->mhpmax)
            mtmp->mhp = mtmp->mhpmax;
        else mtmp->mhp += imv;

(imv is the time spent elsewhere.))

